IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332), Part V: reg 88, payment of benefits pending a coverage decision.
-- Piece er5, LAYER 1: the law, objectively. Every `src:N` is a line of SOR-96-332.txt. The text is an unofficial rendering;
-- nothing here is claimed to be verified against the official text.
--
-- Relation (Hohfeld): the claimant's claim to be paid benefits for hours that are the subject of a ruling is suspended; the
-- other side is the Commission's (and the Minister's) no-duty to pay until the day the rulings are final.
-- The request for a ruling is made under s 90(1)(a) to (d) of the Act, the appeal to the Tax Court under s 103: both are piece ei3's.
-- The text names the "Canada Customs and Revenue Agency", an agency whose name the text has not updated; it is carried as the text writes it.

§ `Regulations Part V - Payment of Benefits Pending a Coverage Decision`

§§ `Reg 88(1)(a) and (b) - the day the rulings become final`

-- One dispute over insurable hours can pass through up to four further stages after the officer's ruling: (i) an appeal to the Minister of National Revenue,
-- (ii) an appeal to the Tax Court of Canada under s 103, (iii) an application to the Federal Court of Appeal under s 28 of the Federal Courts Act to review
-- and set aside the Tax Court's decision, (iv) an application to the Supreme Court of Canada for leave to appeal. Each exists only "where" it is made.
-- src:1670 | (b) the day on which
-- src:1671 | (i) where an appeal from the ruling of that officer is made to the Minister of National Revenue, the decision of the Minister becomes final,
-- src:1672 | (ii) where an appeal from the decision of the Minister of National Revenue is filed with the Tax Court of Canada pursuant to section 103 of the Act, the decision of the Tax Court becomes final,
-- src:1673 | (iii) where an application is made to the Federal Court of Appeal pursuant to section 28 of the Federal Courts Act to review and set aside the decision of the Tax Court of Canada, the decision of the Federal Court of Appeal becomes final, or
-- src:1674 | (iv) if an application is made to the Supreme Court of Canada for leave to appeal from the decision of the Federal Court of Appeal, the final decision of the Supreme Court of Canada is given.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 88(1)(b) (src:1670-1674)
DECLARE `er5 Stage of a dispute over a ruling` HAS
    `the stage was taken`                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day on which the decision at that stage becomes final` IS A MAYBE DATE -- NOTHING while the decision is not yet final

-- Benefits are not payable "until the later of (a) the day on which the officer's ruling on the question becomes final; and (b) the day on which"
-- the decision at each stage that was taken becomes final. The answer is the latest of those days, and NOTHING while the officer's ruling or any stage taken is not yet final.
-- src:1668 | 88 (1) Subject to subsection (2), where a request is made to an officer of the Canada Customs and Revenue Agency under paragraph 90(1)(a), (b), (c) or (d) of the Act for a ruling on the question of whether a claimant is or was employed in insurable employment for any number of hours in a particular period of employment or alleged employment, no benefits are payable in respect of any hour that is the subject of the ruling until the later of
-- src:1669 | (a) the day on which the officer's ruling on the question becomes final; and
-- src:1670 | (b) the day on which
-- src:1671 | (i) where an appeal from the ruling of that officer is made to the Minister of National Revenue, the decision of the Minister becomes final,
-- src:1672 | (ii) where an appeal from the decision of the Minister of National Revenue is filed with the Tax Court of Canada pursuant to section 103 of the Act, the decision of the Tax Court becomes final,
-- src:1673 | (iii) where an application is made to the Federal Court of Appeal pursuant to section 28 of the Federal Courts Act to review and set aside the decision of the Tax Court of Canada, the decision of the Federal Court of Appeal becomes final, or
-- src:1674 | (iv) if an application is made to the Supreme Court of Canada for leave to appeal from the decision of the Federal Court of Appeal, the final decision of the Supreme Court of Canada is given.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 88(1) (src:1668-1674)
GIVEN `the day on which the officer's ruling on the question becomes final` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the appeal to the Minister of National Revenue` IS A `er5 Stage of a dispute over a ruling`
      `the appeal to the Tax Court of Canada under section 103 of the Act` IS A `er5 Stage of a dispute over a ruling`
      `the application to the Federal Court of Appeal under section 28 of the Federal Courts Act` IS A `er5 Stage of a dispute over a ruling`
      `the application to the Supreme Court of Canada for leave to appeal` IS A `er5 Stage of a dispute over a ruling`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `reg 88(1) the later of the day the officer's ruling becomes final and the day the decision at the last stage taken becomes final` IS
    CONSIDER `the day on which the officer's ruling on the question becomes final`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST ruling THEN
        IF any (GIVEN s YIELD isNothing (`er5 reg 88 final day of` s)) `the stages taken`
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE JUST (Date (maximum ((Day ruling) FOLLOWED BY (map (GIVEN s YIELD Day (fromMaybe ruling (`er5 reg 88 final day of` s))) `the stages taken`))))
    WHERE
        `the stages taken` MEANS
            filter (GIVEN s YIELD `er5 reg 88 stage taken` s)
                   (LIST `the appeal to the Minister of National Revenue`,
                         `the appeal to the Tax Court of Canada under section 103 of the Act`,
                         `the application to the Federal Court of Appeal under section 28 of the Federal Courts Act`,
                         `the application to the Supreme Court of Canada for leave to appeal`)

-- Reading helpers for the record above (a genitive on a bracketed application does not parse, so each field is read in a rule that takes the record).
GIVEN stage IS A `er5 Stage of a dispute over a ruling`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `er5 reg 88 stage taken` IS stage's `the stage was taken`

GIVEN stage IS A `er5 Stage of a dispute over a ruling`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `er5 reg 88 final day of` IS stage's `the day on which the decision at that stage becomes final`

§§ `Reg 88(2) - when subsection (1) does not apply`

-- src:1675 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the claimant qualifies to receive benefits under the Act on the basis of hours of insurable employment other than the hours that are the subject of the application.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 88(2) (src:1675)
GIVEN `the claimant qualifies to receive benefits under the Act on the basis of hours of insurable employment other than the hours that are the subject of the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 88(2) subsection 88(1) does not apply` IF
    `the claimant qualifies to receive benefits under the Act on the basis of hours of insurable employment other than the hours that are the subject of the application`

§§ `Reg 88(1) - no benefits payable for the hours that are the subject of the ruling`

-- "Subject to subsection (2), where a request is made to an officer ... under paragraph 90(1)(a), (b), (c) or (d) of the Act for a ruling on the question
-- of whether a claimant is or was employed in insurable employment for any number of hours in a particular period of employment or alleged employment,
-- no benefits are payable in respect of any hour that is the subject of the ruling until the later of (a) and (b)."
-- The day that the later of (a) and (b) names is itself payable: "until" is read as "not before" that day (assumed, not ruled: fork F-reg88).
-- While any stage is not yet final the day is NOTHING and benefits are not payable on any day.
-- src:1668 | 88 (1) Subject to subsection (2), where a request is made to an officer of the Canada Customs and Revenue Agency under paragraph 90(1)(a), (b), (c) or (d) of the Act for a ruling on the question of whether a claimant is or was employed in insurable employment for any number of hours in a particular period of employment or alleged employment, no benefits are payable in respect of any hour that is the subject of the ruling until the later of
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 88(1) (src:1668)
GIVEN `a request has been made to an officer of the Canada Customs and Revenue Agency under paragraph 90(1)(a), (b), (c) or (d) of the Act for a ruling on whether the claimant is or was employed in insurable employment for any number of hours` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the hour is one of the hours that is the subject of the ruling` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant qualifies to receive benefits on the basis of hours of insurable employment other than the hours that are the subject of the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the later of the rulings becomes final` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 88(1) no benefits are payable in respect of the hour on the day in question` IF
        `a request has been made to an officer of the Canada Customs and Revenue Agency under paragraph 90(1)(a), (b), (c) or (d) of the Act for a ruling on whether the claimant is or was employed in insurable employment for any number of hours`
    AND `the hour is one of the hours that is the subject of the ruling`
    AND (NOT (`reg 88(2) subsection 88(1) does not apply` `the claimant qualifies to receive benefits on the basis of hours of insurable employment other than the hours that are the subject of the application`))
    AND (   CONSIDER `the day on which the later of the rulings becomes final`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
            WHEN JUST final THEN `the day in question` BELOW final)
